    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d3-a1">

                <pb facs="0045" n="12" sameAs="frus:frus1969-76v23/pg12"/>


                <p>1. What is the role of the Middle East today in U.S. global strategy? What are
                    the real U.S. interests there and how important are they?</p>
                <p>2. What is the nature of the Soviet threat to the Middle East? How likely is
                    Soviet dominance or predominance? What forces will tend to limit Soviet
                    influence?</p>
                <p>3. What is the precise nature of the Soviet threat to NATO via the Middle
                    East?</p>
                <p>4. What is the present state of the U.S. position in the Middle East? Is it
                    eroding drastically? Or is there a level of common interests shared with some
                    nations in the area which will prevent it from deteriorating beyond a certain
                    point? Is an early Arab-Israel settlement essential to preserving the U.S.
                    position?</p>
                <p>5. In the light of answers to these questions, what is the most appropriate U.S.
                    posture toward the Middle East? What level and kinds of involvement are
                    appropriate in view of our interests and U.S. and Soviet capabilities?</p>
            </div>
        </body>
